# Board branches: <board> <base mirror branch> <flatten>
# mica/<board> is the base plus the board's commits. tools/sync.sh replays those commits onto the
# synced base and cuts mica/<board>-<date>. flatten=yes: the base's submodules are vendored into
# the tree by one commit (trailer Mica-Flatten: <base>) before the board's commits, because those
# commits change files inside the submodules. A board whose mica/<board> does not exist yet is skipped.
